A thread destroyed while another core's trap for it is marked to be dropped leaves the mark,
so a core woken with nothing to run keeps it, to drop a trap of the next thread it runs:
the mark goes with the turn it was set for.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a core is to drop a trap it is not taking

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -182,7 +182,6 @@ void core_thread_gone(const struct thread *t)
         /* The trap finds no thread, and drops what it was for all the same. */
         if (c->turn == t) {
             c->turn = NULL;
-            c->drop_trap = false;
         }
         /* The turn it paid for may be left on spare time, which a thread with time waiting there takes. */
         if (c->payer == t) {
